{%- comment -%}
  Cart drawer — the whole cart UI.

  Rendered once per page from sections/ness-cart-drawer.liquid, which is pulled
  into layout/theme.liquid with a static {% section %} tag. That section exists
  purely so this markup can be re-rendered through the Section Rendering API
  (`/?sections=ness-cart-drawer`) after every cart mutation — the Liquid below
  stays the single source of truth for the drawer's markup, and ness-cart.js
  never hand-builds a line item.

  Progressive enhancement, in three parts:

  1. The drawer starts closed via the `hidden` *attribute* (not a CSS rule), so
     a blocked stylesheet cannot leave it covering the page. It is opened only
     by ness-cart.js.
  2. Nothing here is the only route to the cart. The header's cart pill is a
     real link to /cart; ness-cart.js intercepts the click and opens this
     instead. With JavaScript off the shopper lands on the cart page, which is
     the same cart.
  3. Every control inside is a real form or link — the quantity buttons POST to
     /cart/change, Remove is `item.url_to_remove`, Checkout POSTs to /cart. The
     script upgrades those to fetch calls; it does not invent them.

  Line item properties are displayed, not just carried. Processing Time and
  Pickup Option drive fulfilment (PLAN.md, "Line item properties"), so a
  shopper must be able to see what they chose before paying.

  Only [data-cart-content] is swapped on re-render, so the host element, the
  overlay, and the live region survive and keep their listeners.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  The announcement is composed here rather than in JavaScript so the wording
  lives with the rest of the drawer's copy. strip_html guards against currency
  formats whose `money` output carries markup.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture cart_announce -%}
  {%- if cart.item_count == 0 -%}
    Your bag is now empty.
  {%- else -%}
    Your bag, {{ cart.item_count }} item{% if cart.item_count != 1 %}s{% endif %}, subtotal {{ cart.total_price | money }}.
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

<ness-cart-drawer id="ness-cart-drawer" hidden>
  <button
    type="button"
    class="ness-overlay"
    data-cart-overlay
    tabindex="-1"
    aria-hidden="true"
  ></button>

  <aside
    class="ness-cart"
    data-cart-panel
    role="dialog"
    aria-modal="true"
    aria-labelledby="ness-cart-title"
  >
    <div
      class="ness-cart__inner"
      data-cart-content
      data-item-count="{{ cart.item_count }}"
      data-announce="{{ cart_announce | strip_html | strip | escape }}"
    >
      <div class="ness-cart__head">
        <h2 class="ness-cart__title" id="ness-cart-title">
          Your bag{% if cart.item_count > 0 %} ({{ cart.item_count }}){% endif %}
        </h2>
        <button
          type="button"
          class="ness-cart__close"
          data-cart-close
          data-focus-key="close"
          aria-label="Close bag"
        >
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" stroke="#15001A" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
            <path d="M1 1L15 15M15 1L1 15" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          </svg>
        </button>
      </div>

      <div class="ness-cart__body">
        {%- if cart.item_count == 0 -%}
          <div class="ness-cart__empty">
            <p>Your bag is empty.</p>
            <a
              class="ness-cart__cta"
              href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}"
              data-focus-key="shop"
            >
              Start Shopping
            </a>
          </div>
        {%- else -%}
          {%- for item in cart.items -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              Properties are captured first so the <dl> is only emitted when at
              least one survives filtering — an empty definition list read out
              as "list, 0 items" is noise. Shopify's own hidden properties are
              prefixed with an underscore and are skipped.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- capture item_properties -%}
              {%- for property in item.properties -%}
                {%- assign property_first_char = property.first | slice: 0 -%}
                {%- if property.last != blank and property_first_char != '_' -%}
                  <div class="ness-cart__prop">
                    <dt class="ness-cart__prop-name">{{ property.first | escape }}:</dt>
                    <dd class="ness-cart__prop-value">
                      {%- if property.last contains '/uploads/' -%}
                        <a
                          href="{{ property.last | escape }}"
                          target="_blank"
                          rel="noopener"
                          aria-describedby="a11y-new-window-message"
                        >
                          {{- property.last | split: '/' | last | escape -}}
                        </a>
                      {%- else -%}
                        {{- property.last | escape -}}
                      {%- endif -%}
                    </dd>
                  </div>
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            {%- endcapture -%}

            {%- assign item_title = item.product.title | escape -%}
            {%- assign decreased_quantity = item.quantity | minus: 1 -%}
            {%- assign increased_quantity = item.quantity | plus: 1 -%}

            {%- comment -%}
              At a quantity of one the decrease button removes the line, so it
              says so rather than promising to decrease something that cannot
              go lower.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- if item.quantity == 1 -%}
              {%- capture decrease_label -%}Remove {{ item_title }} from your bag{%- endcapture -%}
            {%- else -%}
              {%- capture decrease_label -%}Decrease quantity of {{ item_title }}{%- endcapture -%}
            {%- endif -%}

            <div class="ness-cart__line">
              {%- comment -%}
                The thumbnail repeats the link beside it, so it is hidden from
                assistive technology and taken out of the tab order — the line
                appears once in a screen reader's link list, not twice.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <a class="ness-cart__media" href="{{ item.url }}" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
                {%- if item.image -%}
                  {{
                    item.image
                    | image_url: width: 264
                    | image_tag:
                      class: 'ness-cart__image',
                      alt: '',
                      width: 88,
                      height: 117,
                      widths: '88, 132, 176, 264',
                      sizes: '88px',
                      loading: 'lazy'
                  }}
                {%- else -%}
                  {{ 'product-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'ness-cart__image ness-cart__image--placeholder' }}
                {%- endif -%}
              </a>

              <div class="ness-cart__info">
                <div class="ness-cart__text">
                  <a class="ness-cart__name" href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item_title }}</a>

                  {%- unless item.product.has_only_default_variant -%}
                    <p class="ness-cart__variant">
                      {%- for option in item.options_with_values -%}
                        {{- option.value | escape -}}
                        {%- unless forloop.last %} &middot; {% endunless -%}
                      {%- endfor -%}
                    </p>
                  {%- endunless -%}

                  {%- if item.selling_plan_allocation -%}
                    <p class="ness-cart__variant">
                      {{- item.selling_plan_allocation.selling_plan.name | escape -}}
                    </p>
                  {%- endif -%}

                  {%- if item_properties != blank -%}
                    <dl class="ness-cart__props">{{ item_properties }}</dl>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </div>

                <div class="ness-cart__controls">
                  {%- comment -%}
                    A real POST to /cart/change. The quantity travels on the
                    button that was pressed, so there is exactly one `quantity`
                    in the payload and no JavaScript is needed to decide the
                    direction. ness-cart.js intercepts the click and sends the
                    same pair to /cart/change.js instead.
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  <form
                    class="ness-cart__qty"
                    action="{{ routes.cart_change_url }}"
                    method="post"
                    data-cart-change
                  >
                    <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ item.key }}">
                    <button
                      type="submit"
                      class="ness-cart__qty-btn"
                      name="quantity"
                      value="{{ decreased_quantity }}"
                      data-cart-qty
                      data-line="{{ item.key }}"
                      data-focus-key="dec:{{ item.key }}"
                      aria-label="{{ decrease_label }}"
                    >
                      &minus;
                    </button>
                    <span class="ness-cart__qty-value">
                      <span class="visually-hidden">Quantity:</span>
                      {{ item.quantity }}
                    </span>
                    <button
                      type="submit"
                      class="ness-cart__qty-btn"
                      name="quantity"
                      value="{{ increased_quantity }}"
                      data-cart-qty
                      data-line="{{ item.key }}"
                      data-focus-key="inc:{{ item.key }}"
                      aria-label="Increase quantity of {{ item_title }}"
                    >
                      +
                    </button>
                  </form>

                  <span class="ness-cart__line-price">
                    {%- if item.original_line_price != item.final_line_price -%}
                      <s class="ness-cart__line-price-was">
                        <span class="visually-hidden">Regular price</span>
                        {{ item.original_line_price | money }}
                      </s>
                      <span>
                        <span class="visually-hidden">Sale price</span>
                        {{ item.final_line_price | money }}
                      </span>
                    {%- else -%}
                      {{ item.final_line_price | money }}
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </span>

                  {%- comment -%}
                    A link, not a button: url_to_remove is a working URL, so
                    Remove keeps working if the script never runs.
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  <a
                    class="ness-cart__remove"
                    href="{{ item.url_to_remove }}"
                    data-cart-remove
                    data-line="{{ item.key }}"
                    data-focus-key="rm:{{ item.key }}"
                    aria-label="Remove {{ item_title }} from your bag"
                  >
                    Remove
                  </a>
                </div>

                {%- if item.line_level_discount_allocations.size > 0 -%}
                  <ul class="ness-cart__discounts" role="list" aria-label="Discounts">
                    {%- for discount in item.line_level_discount_allocations -%}
                      <li>
                        {{- discount.discount_application.title | escape }} (&minus;{{ discount.amount | money }})
                      </li>
                    {%- endfor -%}
                  </ul>
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
            </div>
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- if cart.item_count > 0 -%}
        <div class="ness-cart__foot">
          {%- if cart.cart_level_discount_applications.size > 0 -%}
            <ul class="ness-cart__discounts" role="list" aria-label="Discounts">
              {%- for discount in cart.cart_level_discount_applications -%}
                <li>
                  {{- discount.title | escape }} (&minus;{{ discount.total_allocated_amount | money }})
                </li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          {%- endif -%}

          <div class="ness-cart__totals">
            <span class="ness-cart__subtotal-label">Subtotal</span>
            <span class="ness-cart__subtotal-value">{{ cart.total_price | money }}</span>
          </div>

          <p class="ness-cart__note">Taxes and shipping calculated at checkout.</p>

          <form action="{{ routes.cart_url }}" method="post" class="ness-cart__checkout">
            <button
              type="submit"
              name="checkout"
              class="ness-cart__cta ness-cart__cta--block"
              data-focus-key="checkout"
            >
              Checkout
            </button>
          </form>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Inside the dialog, and outside [data-cart-content].

    Both halves matter. aria-modal="true" prunes everything outside the dialog
    from the accessibility tree, so a live region placed as a sibling of the
    <aside> is never announced — which silently removed all feedback from
    quantity changes and removals for screen reader users. And a live region
    that is itself removed and re-inserted by a re-render is not reliably
    announced either, so it stays out of the replaced subtree.
  {%- endcomment -%}
    <p class="visually-hidden" data-cart-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
  </aside>
</ness-cart-drawer>
